 heroes  and i hope will be heroes again  it is a heroic thing i believe to find  the facts  and tell the truth especially when those  truths are  unpopular and inconvenient  in recent years the word gatekeeper has  taken on a negative connotation  one that i believe is wholly undeserved  there was a reason why so many of the  cities and towns of the ancient and  medieval worlds were walled  and it was not to provide picturesque  ruins for tourists to stroll upon  the night was dark and full of terrors  and the gatekeepers  the guards were there to keep them out  today's social media have given us a  world largely without gatekeepers  and the trolls have all come out from  under the bridges to bedevils  our divisions go deeper and more  rancorous every year  there is so much information so much  misinformation out there  so many falsehoods and as edgar ellen  poe once said  a lie travels around the world while the  truth  is putting her boots on how can we hope  to come together again  to trust with facts  i say that is where it all begins i  never wanted a journalist to tell me  what to  think i could think for myself just  give me the facts does that sound easy  far from it it was never easy and it  grows harder every year  a few years after my own graduation when  i had finally reached a point where i  had a little disposable income  i made what was for me an extravagant  purchase  i bought a set of the encyclopedia  britannica  all that knowledge in one place an  essential tool for  any writer the other essential tools  being a good dictionary how to lie with  statistics  and the elements of style by strunk and  white  that encyclopedia served me well for a  long long time  but a while back observing the dust that  had gathered on top of the books  i came to the realization that had been  years since i had last opened the volume  a larger repository of human knowledge  had displaced it  the internet these days like most of the  human race when i need to know something  i google it's so much quicker so much  easier  and there's more information to be found  online than in all the encyclopedias  ever printed  put together and that would be wonderful  if only so much of it was not well  wrong those of you who have been paying  attention may have noticed that i have  returned three times to that quote about  a lie traveling halfway around the world  what truth is putting on  its pants or sneakers or boots  words that i have variously attributed  to winston churchill  to mark twain to edgar allan poe  who actually said that you may ask all  of the above perhaps  try none of the above  the line is most often attributed to  mark twain but according to quote  investigator.com  it does not turn up in any of his  writings and there is no record of him  ever having uttered those words during  any of his speeches  churchill never said it and poe really  does that sound like poe to you if a lie  was traveling around the world in pose  time it was traveling by horseback  these days lies travel at the speed of  light thanks to the internet  that's where i found all of these uh  what shall we call them misquotations  you can find them too they're still  there just type in a paraphrase of the  saying with quote  and it will all pop up with little  pictures of whoever is being credit  being given credit for saying those  words they are  wrong mind you but they're still there  and there they will remain for years  for decades for centuries  a thousand years to now if humanity has  spread to the stars some future internet  will tell us that mark twain once said  oh i will jump to the horse head nebula  while truth is putting on a space suit  the internet is forever its errors are  forever the internet is the greatest  depository of human knowledge in the  long  sordid and glorious history of our race  but is also home of the big lie  and a thousand little lies along with  millions of innocent mistakes fumbles  and bumbles we should do better we can  do better  we have to do better if we ever hope to  build a better world  you cannot build on a foundation of  mistruths  will we do better that i think is up to  you  and all the other young men and women  leaving college around the nation and  the world  my generation the class of 1971 had the  specter of vietnam  hanging over us as we left campus your  generation  faces a different sort of struggle a war  for truth  for facts for the soul of a nation  in the words of another of my heroes  stan lee  with great power comes great  responsibility  good luck to all of you  thank you  you
 

